WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
REVENGE

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.450
Why didn't you wake me up?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.540
I told you we had an important
meeting with my father!

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:12.460
Why didn't you have your wife
give you a wake-up call, then?

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:13.800
Dammit!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.550
Why didn't you wake me up?

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.840
My apologies, sir.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.970
You idiots are the reason my abilities
are brought into question.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.480
I'm no pushover, you hear me!

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.060
I could have you fired with
a snap of my fingers!

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.610
Good morning, President Chen.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.120
Get moving! My grandfather
will be there today too!

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.580
My best friend's death has given me
a chance to redeem myself.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.420
I'm not going to waste it.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.380
Hey! What did you stop for?

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.680
Who the hell...?!

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.180
That's it. Just stay right there.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.310
Step on it!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.440
You, lock the door.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.030
Release your butterfly, Meiling.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:21.950
Your work hasn't been going well
recently, so I hear.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.950
Must be tough being a no-good son.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.130
So, you allowed some Beijing nouveau riche

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:37.300
to steal our distribution channels
in Japan?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.170
But Father, whichever way you look at it
there's something not right here.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.800
Counselor Zhou is
one of my oldest friends!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.560
There's no way he'd sell out to a bunch
of people he barely knows!

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.810
He's nothing more than a traitor.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.940
Father, wait!
He's just had his first child!

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.990
So what?

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.030
He was only ever a close friend of yours,

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.790
and this is what happened
because you trusted him.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.200
You're a total pushover!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.750
Meiling, what do you think
you're doing?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.710
Change his memories now
or your butterfly's gonna burn.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.600
Please don't.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:31.350
Don't burn Meiling's butterfly.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.730
If you don't want it to burn,
stop fooling around!

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.320
I think you had better start
worrying about yourself

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.740
rather than about your friend.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.240
W...What do you mean?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:53.620
Your grandfather says we should
take you out for being a traitor as well.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.540
That can't be...

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.500
Grandfather wouldn't say such a thing.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.750
Indeed. It's a crazy demand.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.010
No sane person would ask to have
their own grandson whacked.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:08.390
It seems your grandfather is
growing senile in his old age.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:15.100
But so long as he's head of the family,
we have no choice but to obey him.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.610
I want to help you, do you hear me?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.610
That's not all.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:26.400
At this rate, the family will lose
not only its status but its fortune,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.160
which is why we have to take action now.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.910
Dahao, you must kill
your grandfather.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.170
I have to... kill my grandfather.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.670
Meiling, you can return the butterfly.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:48.180
I have to... kill my grandfather.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.510
That's the only way for you to be saved.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.560
It's also in your family's best interests.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.440
You ready? When I click
my fingers, that'll be the signal.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.070
Make sure you finish the job.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:08.240
For the sake of my life...

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.450
For the sake of the family...

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.120
We'll have to rebuild this dude too.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:18.460
This would've been easier
if Jin had been around.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:32.850
Don't look!

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:37.100
Don't look where it's burning!
Come here, butterfly!

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:39.480
Come back to me!

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.230
Another one...

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.480
Another bad man...

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.240
Go away!
This is Meiling's house!

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.200
Look at the butterfly, Meiling.

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:05.170
When you're in your house,
only look at the butterfly

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.510
and don't look at the burning flames.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.510
There was so much burning,
it was so scary...

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.050
I'm sorry, Meiling.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.470
There's no other way but
for you to look at the butterfly.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:20.020
But I promise I'll come back
for you, one day.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.860
Mister... come back soon.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.410
Hey! Why have you stopped?
Get moving!

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:46.670
Hey, Katsuragi. Word on the street is
Tsukasa's been crushed.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:48.250
That's right.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.470
Katsuragi. Help me carry Tsukasa upstairs.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.560
You've got yourself in quite the pickle.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:07:59.600
Who're you?

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.770
He doesn't understand Mandarin, Mr. Long.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:03.560
I know.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.320
Hey, don't look so glum, chum.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.700
I'll be taking care of you from now on.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.040
It's been a while, Long.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.380
You don't have to stand up, Tsukasa.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.550
I'm glad you're safe!
I was beginning to worry.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.050
I'm a bit busy right now.
Can you come back some other day?

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:40.810
Sure.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.810
I've got to get back and
report this anyway.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.650
Say, Tsukasa. There was
some girl in the car with him...

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.320
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:56.240
-I'm okay.
-You're clearly not!

00:08:56.530 --> 00:09:00.410
Katsuragi, don't just stand there. Help!
Hold onto his feet.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.580
Don't hit anything!

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:10.630
This really is the "baby" era.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.840
You called me out here, remember.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:18.890
So what do you think you're doing
keeping me waiting?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.680
I'm very sorry.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:24.100
Too busy chasing girls around, I suppose?

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:28.190
Pardon me, sir. The guest's just
been seen pulling into the boatyard.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.610
How many people are with him?

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:33.280
The son and one child.

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:34.860
A child you say?

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.610
I didn't see an escort
and they're unarmed.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:43.750
Has he come to plead for his life with
a kid as a human shield? How desperate.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.500
Okay, bring them here.

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.040
Very well, sir.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.050
Seems he really wants the job in Shanghai.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.130
Impudent punk.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:10:00.050
First, he infiltrates our channels and
now he wants to make friends?

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:04.970
Now that we've got the channels
in Japan back,

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.770
it's probably hard for them
to push product.

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.940
Too late to think about that.

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:14.360
If he wasn't a valuable asset,

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.280
I'd have him fed to the fish
in Inner Port Shelter.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.660
If it comes to that,
it'll be your job, Dahao.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:26.540
It's his fault you've just lost
one of your oldest friends, after all.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:28.040
I understand.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.040
I'll do what has to be done, Father.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.340
What's wrong with you?
You've gone very pale.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.050
The boat has just pulled in.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.550
Check them for firearms
before they board.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.760
No.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.510
Make them remove all their clothes.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.430
He did say they'd be completely open
with us, after all.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:59.240
Long time no see,
ex-President Chen Shengjie.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.490
You know him?

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:04.490
No, I believe today is our first meeting.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:09.500
We did meet a long time ago,
through my father's work.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.000
When was that?
Tell me your father's name!

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.760
You really don't remember, do you?

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:21.010
I suppose not, since my name has changed
along with my appearance.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.890
I am the son of Bai Shichang.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:29.390
He's the son of a qigong master!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.900
I did it. I did it, Father.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.400
What have you done, boy...?

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.660
What do you mean?
I did what you said I should.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.580
This lot are traitors, Mr. President.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:53.040
Okay. I'll just have to keep a lookout
and make sure no more traitors come.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.840
Shoot them, Dahao!

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:04.680
There's a good boy. You did well.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.100
Now go to sleep.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.680
You're a qigong master, aren't you!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:15.690
We wiped out those obsolete relics
a long time ago.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.690
You remember, right...?

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:23.400
It was just after you got some of them
to kill my father.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.530
I've waited 18 years for this moment.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:31.750
Staying alive all this time just to see
you witness your own father's death.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.170
Tell me, now. How does it feel?

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.420
Meiling, release your butterfly.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:42.670
I'll have you work for me
for the rest of your life.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.060
This locus is home to the best memories
of a certain person

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.140
who used to look after me.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.730
But I can't remember who it was anymore.

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:00.360
The breeze feels wonderful, though.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:03.110
I don't feel scared when I'm here.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:05.530
You can stay here for a while too.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:10.450
So you like the water, do you?
It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:15.960
The water in this river runs down
from that mountain in the distance.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.290
And it flows for miles and miles.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.260
Until it finally reaches the vast ocean.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.380
You too will someday leave this locus,

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:28.260
and go into the vast world outside.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.760
Scoop up a little.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:47.860
Get out of this place, Tsukasa!

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:55.000
Tsukasa. Keep it together!

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.540
Hiroki.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.630
You okay? You woke up screaming again.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.260
Crap. Why won't you eat what I feed you?

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.890
This isn't the time to be fighting.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:16.770
Crud. It's Tsukasa's feeding time too.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:21.150
Three days from now. No problem.
I'll get my pet to do it.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.070
He'll definitely do it if I tell him.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.900
This is your fault anyway
 for shirking your responsibilities.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.530
Hiroki, what are you up to?

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:34.620
What do you think? Bringing your food.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.910
Who was that on the phone?

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:38.540
Mr. Katsuragi.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.670
Why're you two always speaking Chinese?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.130
Stop worrying about it.
It's just a habit we've got into.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.170
Sorry. This must be hard for you.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:52.550
Damn right it is! I already had the fish
to feed and now you as well.

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.680
The long-tailed ones keep fighting
and won't eat their food.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:15:00.560
Sometimes two of the same species start
a turf war if you put them together.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.400
Oh, is that why?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.650
Does that mean I should
put them in different tanks?

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.950
Sorry. I don't think I can eat.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.450
Is it that unappetizing?

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.700
That's not it.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:18.330
Anything slightly slimy isn't going
to go down well for some time...

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.170
Oh, right... Of course not.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:27.800
I'll get some pancakes on the go,
dripping with lots of dark honey.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.090
Hiroki.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:31.510
You must be overwhelmed.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.470
Why don't we move to a hotel?

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:37.970
You want to be in the Company's pocket
again? After all they did to you!

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.350
You can count me out! I never want
to see you in that state again!

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:46.860
I'm not doing anything for those assholes!
Nor am I letting you work for them.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.280
I'm afraid I will be working for them.

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:52.240
In fact, that last phone call
was about the next job.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:57.290
I can't do it in this condition.
So, I have to ask you to do it for me.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.000
Are you kidding me, Tsukasa?!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:04.170
I nearly saw you get crushed
without so much as an explanation!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.880
Explaining it all wouldn't have achieved
anything other than worrying you.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:11.630
Are you telling me you knew
the risk and still did it?

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.050
You would've been crushed
if I hadn't been there.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.270
What would happen to me
if you got crushed!

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:23.020
You really don't care about me, do you?

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:29.280
Why won't you talk to me? You've never
even told me about your peak giver.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:31.650
Do you not trust me or something?

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:37.160
Trust only lasts until someone involved
changes their mind.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.160
What...?

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:43.330
I've spent my life thinking I couldn't
survive unless someone needed me

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:47.460
I was raised by the Company
for the organ trade.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:51.670
If my peak giver hadn't found me,

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.340
my organs would've been
taken out and sold off.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.800
But because the Company saw
I had the ability, they let me live...

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.310
You and I are different, Hiroki.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:04.940
I looked for you and found you.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:08.060
You were needed from the very beginning.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.360
But not me.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:14.200
My necessity was forever being tested.

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:18.700
So I did whatever I was asked
to try and prove my worth.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:22.500
Who cares about the Company now, though?

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:25.460
Let's quit and start a life for ourselves.

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.040
Hiroki...

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:31.710
There's no retiring from this business...

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.090
Why on earth not?

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.760
I think I need a rest.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.140
You know my fish tank locus, right?

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:49.150
There's a goldfish
I'd like to put in there.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.990
You sure you're okay
to sync like this, Tsukasa?

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.450
I don't think I'll be able
to hold it too long.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:02.620
Why here though?

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.620
The apartment might be bugged.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.120
Bugged?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.420
I told you we were being watched, right?

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:12.250
If we ever ran away from the Company,

00:18:12.460 --> 00:18:14.670
they'd come after us for sure.

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.510
They wouldn't stop until we were dead.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:21.010
So you're saying we have to do
the Company's bidding forever?

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.760
Not exactly. Listen...

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.390
The Company needs us more than ever.

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.770
We can use that to our advantage.

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:33.020
It'll soon be our turn to make
the Company do what we want.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:37.860
We need to start giving conditions
under which we're willing to work.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.740
That way we'll be able to live
our lives as we wish.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.240
But, I said I didn't want
to work for them...

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:47.040
You have to a little longer.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.210
But there's a way...

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.170
A way for us not to do jobs we hate,
by just sharing our peaks.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:57.300
Sharing our peaks?

00:18:57.800 --> 00:18:59.720
There's something I want
to show you, Hiroki.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:03.800
Once you see it, you'll understand
everything I've been saying.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:06.470
And when can I see that?

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:09.020
The Company has it now...

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.150
But I will show it to you someday.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.360
So you only have to work a little longer.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:16.860
Hiroki,

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:21.450
this is sure to work if you
and I do it together. Trust me.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:25.740
What? But you just said
I shouldn't rely on trust.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.410
You can rely on me.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.330
You can rely on me too, dammit!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:34.460
I do rely on you.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:37.460
You're the only one I don't want
to be betrayed by, Hiroki.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.170
Why would I betray you?

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.720
So you'll go along with my plan, then?

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:47.220
Fine. If that's what you want.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.230
I'll help with the jobs.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:54.020
Sorry. I think this is my limit.
Let's pull out.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:19:59.610
-You okay?
-Yeah.

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:03.360
So, I can rely on you, Hiroki?

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.070
Keep this quiet.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:07.370
Of course I will.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.040
I'm relying on your pancakes too...

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.380
Is that right? Okay.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.380
Got it. I'll make sure
they're dripping with dark honey.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.090
It's called maple syrup, Hiroki...

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:22.300
I know that!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.890
That damn Tsukasa,

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:29.100
trying to pretend he's fine
when he's obviously not.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.390
Is he that desperate to prove himself?

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:32.770
But...

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.900
this makes Tsukasa a "son",
holding the same rank as us.

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.980
That's true. But you know, Jin...

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.650
It just makes me hate him even more.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.200
You saw Hayashi's personal effects, right?

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:48.910
Hayashi had a bond with Tsukasa too.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:54.790
Just one order from the top, and Tsukasa
crushed a man who treated him like family.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:21:01.050
You haven't forgotten what
bastards like that did to us, have you?

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.380
I have Hiroki.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:08.260
With Hiroki by my side, I'm sure
 I can start again from scratch.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:12.810
Start from scratch...
 Start what?

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:18.110
I need to tell Hiroki
 everything about the "babies".

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:22.940
The Company needs people
 who can create "babies".

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.070
And that's why...

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.330
Satoru's got to go.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:33.830
What's in this honey that
makes it maple syrup anyway?

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.960
Man, those pancakes smell great.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:38.960
Hey, Satoru! What's that hairdo about?

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.960
-You look like a chimp!
-A chimp?

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.380
You're dyeing yours next, Hiroki.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.130
What?

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.840
You can't look like that for the next job.

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:51.100
You're dyeing it and cutting that fringe
or combing it back.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:52.720
You're kidding me, right?

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:54.850
I am not "kidding you"!

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.600
You've dyed yours too, Tsukasa?

00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:00.610
I might have gone a bit too far.
I'll try again.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:04.030
Yeah, you might want a bit more color.

00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.400
Make Hiroki dye his hair, Tsukasa.

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:09.490
God damn... Well, I prefer how
Tsukasa's hair looks now, anyway.

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:11.580
Hey, what's this doing here?

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:15.120
Ah, crap! I was supposed
to separate those two.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:18.870
One of them is dead, man...

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
Artist: Mari Yamazaki
